# TypeScript patterns

## Module boundaries

- Domain logic in `src/lib/<domain>/` — pure functions, testable at public seams
- Hooks in `src/hooks/` — thin adapters over lib modules
- UI in `src/routes/` and `src/components/` — no business rules buried in JSX

## Custom hooks

Extract hooks when the same state/effect sequence appears in 2+ components. Keep hooks focused.

## Repository / adapter pattern

Persist through adapters (memory, Supabase). Domain modules depend on interfaces, not Supabase directly.

## API responses

Prefer typed results over throwing for expected failures at boundaries:

```typescript
type Result<T> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: string }
```

## Domain language

Match test names and public API vocabulary to `CONTEXT.md`. Read relevant ADRs before changing behaviour.
